 "text": "Hey there, how are you? That's a lot. Do you send out an invitation only email every year? Go ahead. Lots of people still use email for invitations, no matter how many people you invite. It means you should send out an annual invite so people know they should save the date. If you wait until next year, you'll end up with half the attendees. Then I' say an annual invite is the way to go. That's fine, just keep it under two hundred. You could always tell the heavy hitters to bring a plus one from work.",
